{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 3873464,
  "courseSlug": "nextjs-react-the-complete-guide",
  "courseTitle": "Next.js & React - The Complete Guide",
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "41161616",
      "title": "Working with Layout Routes",
      "lectureOrder": 40,
      "videoOrder": 38,
      "sourceHash": "bbe66ffc67cde33f53bbde5572c62d665035685371e142642b9fb2fedbaaa1e9",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.1,
          "end": 4.26,
          "en": "When building more complex React apps",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 4.26,
          "end": 7.433,
          "en": "with Routing, it's quite common that some routes should also",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 7.433,
          "end": 10.53,
          "en": "have shared layout elements.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 10.53,
          "end": 14.07,
          "en": "For example, this main navigation bar here at the top,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 14.07,
          "end": 17.91,
          "en": "should probably be visible on all routes we have.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 17.91,
          "end": 20.85,
          "en": "And to achieve this, you can add so-called layout routes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 20.85,
          "end": 23.67,
          "en": "Which are actually just normal routes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 23.67,
          "end": 27.72,
          "en": "but routes that nest other routes inside of them.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 27.72,
          "end": 29.07,
          "en": "To add such a layout route,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 29.07,
          "end": 31.14,
          "en": "we could add a new route definition.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 31.14,
          "end": 33.51,
          "en": "The position in the array doesn't really matter here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 33.51,
          "end": 35.91,
          "en": "but I'll add it as the first route.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 35.91,
          "end": 40.02,
          "en": "And then here the path is still / nothing,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 40.02,
          "end": 42.99,
          "en": "because I want to create a layout that wraps all routes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 42.99,
          "end": 44.973,
          "en": "no matter which path they have.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 46.02,
          "end": 48.75,
          "en": "Then we have to add an element and here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 48.75,
          "end": 51.33,
          "en": "I need to add a new component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 51.33,
          "end": 54.48,
          "en": "And for that I'll actually add a new folder, called routes,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 54.48,
          "end": 57.81,
          "en": "to organize my components differently now.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 57.81,
          "end": 59.85,
          "en": "The components which are used as routes,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 59.85,
          "end": 61.53,
          "en": "should go into the routes folder,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 61.53,
          "end": 64.23,
          "en": "and the other components which are used somewhere else,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 64.23,
          "end": 66.33,
          "en": "will stay in the components folder.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 66.33,
          "end": 68.25,
          "en": "This is not needed technically,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 68.25,
          "end": 71.2,
          "en": "but makes this app a bit easier to maintain and understand.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 72.18,
          "end": 75.99,
          "en": "In this routes folder, I'll add a RootLayout.jsx file,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 75.99,
          "end": 78.75,
          "en": "though the file name, of course, is up to you.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 78.75,
          "end": 81.75,
          "en": "In there, we create a regular component function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 81.75,
          "end": 83.43,
          "en": "which could be called RootLayout,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 83.43,
          "end": 85.383,
          "en": "and which is of course exported.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 86.82,
          "end": 90.87,
          "en": "And then here, I wanna return a fragment",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 90.87,
          "end": 92.673,
          "en": "where I have my MainHeader,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 93.63,
          "end": 96.453,
          "en": "and then something else which I'll add soon.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 97.5,
          "end": 99.99000000000001,
          "en": "For the moment, it's just a MainHeader.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 99.99000000000001,
          "end": 103.25999999999999,
          "en": "And that should be a layout route which is wrapped around",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 103.25999999999999,
          "end": 105.87,
          "en": "other routes so that the MainHeader is shared",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 105.87,
          "end": 107.88,
          "en": "and then the content of the upper routes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 107.88,
          "end": 109.953,
          "en": "is rendered below this MainHeader.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 111.15,
          "end": 113.49000000000001,
          "en": "To make this work, back in main.jsx,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 113.49000000000001,
          "end": 118.49000000000001,
          "en": "we can import the RootLayout route from routes/RootLayout,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 119.07,
          "end": 122.013,
          "en": "and set this as an element here like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 123.6,
          "end": 126.21,
          "en": "And now the important part that must be added here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 126.21,
          "end": 129.42,
          "en": "to make this a layout route, is that we add another key",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 129.42,
          "end": 130.71,
          "en": "to the route definition.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 130.71,
          "end": 133.92,
          "en": "And that's the children key, which takes an array",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 133.92,
          "end": 137.313,
          "en": "and it takes an array of more route definitions.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 138.27,
          "end": 140.812,
          "en": "And here, I'll then move these two route definitions",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 140.812,
          "end": 144.32999999999998,
          "en": "into this RootLayout route definition.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 144.32999999999998,
          "end": 147.407,
          "en": "And that turns this RootLayout route definition",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 147.407,
          "end": 150,
          "en": "into a layout route of these two routes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 150,
          "end": 152.336,
          "en": "Because these two routes are now nested routes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 152.336,
          "end": 156.45,
          "en": "to this route here, and they share the layout provided",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 156.45,
          "end": 158.46,
          "en": "by that route.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 158.46,
          "end": 162.45,
          "en": "They simply are inserted into this RootLayout component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 162.45,
          "end": 164.613,
          "en": "and therefore they share this MainHeader.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 165.66,
          "end": 168.12,
          "en": "However, if we save this you see that, yeah,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 168.12,
          "end": 171,
          "en": "the header is there, but the content is missing,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 171,
          "end": 173.613,
          "en": "and clicking New Post also doesn't do anything.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 174.96,
          "end": 176.76,
          "en": "The reason for that is that indeed,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 176.76,
          "end": 181.08,
          "en": "we are now sharing this MainHeader component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 181.08,
          "end": 184.23,
          "en": "but we're not telling react-router where",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 184.23,
          "end": 187.44,
          "en": "to render the content of these nested routes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 187.44,
          "end": 190.68,
          "en": "And that is of course, something we should do.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 190.68,
          "end": 193.59,
          "en": "And we do that by going to the RootLayout",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 193.59,
          "end": 198.093,
          "en": "and importing an Outlet component from react-router-dom.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 198.99,
          "end": 201,
          "en": "That's a special component provided by",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 201,
          "end": 204,
          "en": "the react-router package, which should be rendered",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 204,
          "end": 208.05,
          "en": "in the place where the actual nested route content",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 208.05,
          "end": 211.053,
          "en": "should be rendered, should be injected, so to say.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 211.95,
          "end": 214.47,
          "en": "So this is simply a placeholder where",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 214.47,
          "end": 217.26,
          "en": "the nested routes can render their content",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 217.26,
          "end": 218.19299999999998,
          "en": "in the RootLayout.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 219.57,
          "end": 221.4,
          "en": "And therefore with Outlet added here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 221.4,
          "end": 223.74,
          "en": "in RootLayout, below the MainHeader,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 223.74,
          "end": 227.554,
          "en": "if we save this, we now got the app component content back.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 227.554,
          "end": 230.73,
          "en": "And therefore, I now also have two headers here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 230.73,
          "end": 233.91,
          "en": "because at the moment, the App component, of course,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 233.91,
          "end": 236.7,
          "en": "still brings its own MainHeader.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 236.7,
          "end": 238.62,
          "en": "But that's what we can tackle next.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 238.62,
          "end": 241.35,
          "en": "It's now time to refactor the code a little bit",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 241.35,
          "end": 243.75,
          "en": "and clean it up a little bit to make sure",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 243.75,
          "end": 246.7,
          "en": "that we don't have this duplicate header here, for example.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
